      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T01:48:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not opposed to exposing bounds functionality in CK. However, the `filterBounds` API is likely going to change (in particular the `MapDirection` parameter and overloaded parameter meanings is problematic). I don\u0027t want to add a new API to CK that just matches an API that will be updated in the next few months.\n\nAnother thing to consider is that with this implementation in CK, `filterBounds()` is only calculating the forward bounds and always with an identity matrix. This is, integer vs. float aside, equivalent to `computeFastBounds()`. I don\u0027t know if CK exposes that on mask filters or SkPaint as an existing precedent to follow?",
      "parentUuid": "da919dbd_105cbb5e",
      "revId": "fd684c55b2ece2a97cad5dc6948e761d239da7fe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "48c34f5d_25022357",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 10154
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T22:31:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For context, Flutter already depends on `SkImageFilter.filterBounds`: https://github.com/flutter/engine/blob/cf2fa190fdc8eee4d8feaa82e21e6e7eb77254b4/lib/web_ui/skwasm/filters.cpp#L58\n\nI\u0027m happy to change this PR to use `SkPaint.computeFastBounds()` if it is equivalent. Basically our only use case for this is to adjust the computed bounds of a picture with the ImageFilter adjustment",
      "parentUuid": "527f3625_6f5ce23b",
      "revId": "fd684c55b2ece2a97cad5dc6948e761d239da7fe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2169f476_213c7e18",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-21T13:47:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The long term API that will be added to SkImageFilter will be\n\n    SkIRect getOutputBounds(const SkMatrix\u0026 ctm, const SkRect\u0026 drawBounds) const;\n    \nand \n   \n    SkIRect getInputBounds(const SkMatrix\u0026 ctm, const SkIRect\u0026 clipBounds, const SkRect\u0026 drawBounds) const;\n    \nThe `ctm` matrix is the full transform of the SkCanvas when the image filter would be used. The `drawBounds` are the local (pre-transformed) bounding box of the geometry being drawn *before* the filter is applied. Both functions return pixel bounding boxes in the canvas device space (post-transformed). For `getInputBounds`, the `clipBounds` is the pixel bounds in device space that can be rendered to.\n\nThe issue for migration is that the old `filterBounds` function expected the input bounding boxes to be in device-space already. For flutter\u0027s use case where they always pass in the identity matrix, it\u0027s a non-issue because mapping from local to device/canvas space is a no-op. In general, it\u0027s probably a good idea to move away from assuming the identity matrix in Flutter\u0027s code simply because it could be misleading about the size of a pixel relative to the local coordinate space.\n\nIn order to future-proof CanvasKit, it would be great if this `filterBounds` function could be updated to match the `getOutputBounds` signature above. Since there is no C++ version of that yet, it can be implemented by calling:\n\n    return filter-\u003efilterBounds(ctm.mapRect(drawBounds).roundOut(), ctm, kForward);\n    \nAnd then Flutter CK would just call that with the identity matrix, just like it does for filterBounds in its skwasm adapter.",
      "parentUuid": "48c34f5d_25022357",
      "revId": "fd684c55b2ece2a97cad5dc6948e761d239da7fe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
